Thus ena[0] (for tens) should be high when ones digit is 9 (i.e., next clock will cause tens increment). Similarly ena[1] high when tens is 9 and ones is 9 (i.e., next clock will cause hundreds increment). ena[2] high when hundreds is 9 and lower digits are 9 (i.e., next clock will cause thousands increment). Or could be high when the digit is about to be incremented (i.e., after lower digit overflow). Implementation details may vary.

